  "term": "taxonomy",
  "definition": "In this context, a taxonomy is an organized way of classifying the factors involved in access to mental healthcare during a public health crisis. It groups related challenges and experiences to help describe how economically marginalized perinatal women and obstetric professionals are affected.",
